# Copy to .env for local development. Never commit real values.
#
# GoHighLevel (LeadConnector) sub-account that receives booking requests from
# the form in src/components/Contact.astro via the server route
# src/pages/api/lead.ts. Create the Private Integration Token under
# Settings → Private Integrations in the sub-account; it needs the
# contacts.write scope (and contacts.readonly for the health check).
GHL_PIT=pit-xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
GHL_LOCATION_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Cloudflare Turnstile — the bot check on the booking form. Create a widget at
# dash.cloudflare.com → Turnstile: widget mode "Managed", hostnames
# hyperdetailing.se and www.hyperdetailing.se, and leave pre-clearance OFF.
# Pre-clearance is what makes Turnstile set a cf_clearance cookie; without it
# the widget only issues a token and the site stays cookie-free, which is why
# it needs no consent banner (see README).
#
# The sitekey is public and ships in the page. The secret is verified
# server-side in src/pages/api/lead.ts and must never reach the browser.
#
# Both are required in production: /api/lead rejects every booking without a
# verified token. Locally you can leave both unset and the check is skipped; to
# exercise it, use Cloudflare's dummy keys (Turnstile docs → Testing).
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY=0x4xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=0x4xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
